WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:05.740
Speaker 1: The Trump writer known in the media
as the Q and on Shaman has been sentenced

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:09.170
to 41 months in prison, and we're going to
talk about the sentence.

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:12.780
We're going to talk about consequences in
general, the way that these court cases are

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:18.260
going and really what the philosophy or approach
should be in terms of sentencing for these

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:22.550
individuals now to step back for a second
and kind of set the stage.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:28.710
There are hundreds of alleged Trump rioters
whose cases are pending right now, and we're

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:34.940
starting to see sentences, sentences that
are very mild, ranging all the way up to several

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:35.940
years.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:39.910
Now, when we talk about consequences for the
Trump riots.

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:45.050
One side of that are the consequences for
individuals that participated people like

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:48.149
the QAnon Shaman, Jacob Chansley and others.

00:00:48.149 --> 00:00:50.110
And we're going to talk about that in a moment.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:53.980
There's a whole other side to consequences,
which has consequences for those that instigated

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:54.980
it.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:01:03.629
Those that created the environment in which
half of the Republican Party or more believed

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:08.460
that the election was actually won by Donald
Trump and that Joe Biden stole it in some

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:09.460
way.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:15.990
And thus it was in some way justified to go
to Washington DC on January 6th and do what

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:17.130
they did.

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:21.590
There have been no consequences for those
people whatsoever, and that includes the former

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:23.130
President Donald Trump himself.

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:25.260
It includes people around Donald Trump.

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:27.369
It includes members of the House of Representatives.

00:01:27.369 --> 00:01:28.850
It includes members of the Senate.

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:30.300
It's a very, very long list.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:35.190
And when we talk about consequences for them,
really, we're probably talking about political

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:36.190
consequences.

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:43.070
I don't think there's any chance, nor arguably
even a legal basis for charges against someone

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:44.070
like me.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.829
And I don't know to pick someone.

00:01:45.829 --> 00:01:50.820
Madison Cawthorn, I don't know, you know,
the people that were going around fomenting

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:51.820
and instigating.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:55.290
There's a question as to whether there will
be political consequences for some of those

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:56.290
people.

00:01:56.290 --> 00:02:01.770
The answer is also probably not, because most
of them are in very red districts, safe districts.

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:06.229
The people in the Senate, many aren't even
up for reelection in 2022.

00:02:06.229 --> 00:02:09.239
So that's one side that's not going particularly
well.

00:02:09.239 --> 00:02:15.010
Now to the sentences and to the news of today,
we're starting to see sentences stack up for

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:17.959
some of these riders on the I think it was
the Monday bonus show.

00:02:17.959 --> 00:02:22.650
We talked about roughly the same amount of
time, about 40 months for one of the other

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:24.180
rioters.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:30.690
One of the most prominent riders is this guy,
Jacob Chansley, known as the Q Shaman.

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:33.650
He has now been sentenced to 41 months.

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:39.010
The man known as QAnon Shaman, who stormed
the Senate chamber on January six, adorned

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:44.549
in face paint and wearing a fur helmet with
horns, was sentenced to 41 months behind bars

00:02:44.549 --> 00:02:45.620
on Wednesday.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:50.739
34 year old Jacob Chansley from Phenix, Arizona,
pleaded guilty in September to one felony

00:02:50.739 --> 00:02:56.439
count of obstruction for his role in trying
to block the counting of the 2020 Electoral

00:02:56.439 --> 00:02:57.620
College votes.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:00.459
He faced up to 20 years in prison on the charge.

00:03:00.459 --> 00:03:04.080
Federal prosecutors themselves had only asked
for 51 months.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:08.200
That was the longest requested sentence so
far in the Trump riots.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:14.310
U.S. District Judge Royce Lamberth handed
down a 41 month sentence and also three years

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:16.489
probation, once released.

00:03:16.489 --> 00:03:21.730
In sentencing, Chansley, Lamberth said he
thought Chansley was quote, Genuine in your

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:25.720
remorse, but the severity of the crime warrants
the sentence.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.110
What you did here was horrific.

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:32.519
As you can now see QAnon Shaman, of course,
as we're showing you here is this guy who's

00:03:32.519 --> 00:03:38.650
shirtless picture wearing the worn fur hat
and the flag and the megaphone and the whole

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:39.650
thing.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:42.879
Images of this guy went viral very, very quickly.

00:03:42.879 --> 00:03:47.260
Videos showed him inside and outside the Capitol
building, yelling at police officers, leading

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:50.930
a mob, eventually getting into the Senate
chamber where he scrawled.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.680
It's only a matter of time.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:57.489
Justice is coming on paper, covering the desk
where Mike Pence had been presiding minutes

00:03:57.489 --> 00:03:59.249
earlier.

00:03:59.249 --> 00:04:04.859
He was in court yesterday with a beard, a
green prison jumpsuit addressed.

00:04:04.859 --> 00:04:11.150
The court referenced Jesus Gandhi and the
movie Shawshank Redemption, expressed remorse

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.379
and said he would do everything differently.

00:04:13.379 --> 00:04:15.319
I was wrong for entering the Capitol.

00:04:15.319 --> 00:04:16.810
I have no excuse.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:18.180
The behavior is indefensible.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:25.380
Now, Chansley asked for a time served, meaning
he gets credit for the time he's already spent

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:29.270
behind bars, saying he's not dangerous, he's
not violent, he's not an insurrectionist or

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:34.400
a domestic terrorist, and he's nothing like
the other people he has been incarcerated

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:35.400
with.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:36.400
So what?

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.470
What's the takeaway here, right?

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:43.060
First of all, there are people who are annoyed
at only 41 months.

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:44.479
A few things to note.

00:04:44.479 --> 00:04:48.120
First of all, the prosecutors only asked for
51 months.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:53.900
So oftentimes we see could be 20 years when
prosecutors say given the circumstances, we're

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:55.479
only asking for 51 months.

00:04:55.479 --> 00:04:57.849
It's rare, not unheard of, but rare.

00:04:57.849 --> 00:05:01.520
Judges sentenced people to more than prosecution
asks for number two.

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:04.969
He did take a guilty plea and he did show
remorse.

00:05:04.969 --> 00:05:07.219
Now we could say the remorse isn't genuine.

00:05:07.219 --> 00:05:15.020
The judge felt that it was, but it is one
of these situations where if he were.

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:20.490
The earlier sentences are increasingly people
who are taking pleas.

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:26.960
It would be reasonable to think that those
who are going to push not guilty maybe go

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:30.509
to trial, et cetera, if they are found guilty.

00:05:30.509 --> 00:05:32.740
We could see even longer sentences.

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:34.380
Trials take longer than please.

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:35.789
All else being equal.

00:05:35.789 --> 00:05:39.050
So we won't know about those sentences for
a period of time.

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:44.580
Also, I got a couple of emails from people
saying, why wasn't this guy charged with treason?

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:47.129
That is very, very difficult.

00:05:47.129 --> 00:05:53.330
And typically prosecutors are not going to
do that unless they are very confident in

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:57.499
the evidence and state of mind is a factor
there.

00:05:57.499 --> 00:05:58.499
Same.

00:05:58.499 --> 00:05:59.669
Same with something like sedition.

00:05:59.669 --> 00:06:01.169
So that's just really tough.

00:06:01.169 --> 00:06:05.340
It's not surprising that the Q and on Shaman
was not charged with treason.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:09.830
Now the Fox News perspective on this, at least
the perspective of Fox News contributor Will

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:15.720
Cain, is that the QAnon Shaman was brainwashed,
I guess, by the left while he was in custody.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:20.580
Speaker 2: Insidious part Tucker he was submitted
to, and he did submit some type of brainwashing.

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:23.009
I mean, they have made all of these.

00:06:23.009 --> 00:06:28.560
Jan. six defendants essentially repent from
any beliefs they ever had an echo critical

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:32.889
race theory ideas, read the right books and
tell a judge they apologize for everyone and

00:06:32.889 --> 00:06:34.449
everything they've ever been.

00:06:34.449 --> 00:06:38.229
It's really gross and it's a violation of
due process, and it's just a violation of

00:06:38.229 --> 00:06:39.229
our sense of justice.

00:06:39.229 --> 00:06:44.439
Speaker 1: Now, I don't know if the references
to Gandhi or whatever were part of that.

00:06:44.439 --> 00:06:49.070
I'm not really sure, but that's what we might
call an alternative perspective.

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:54.879
And that's actually something that's being
repeated a lot by the right, which is these

00:06:54.879 --> 00:06:59.080
alleged insurrectionists are not only being
treated unfairly.

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:02.919
Some of them by being kept detained in pretrial
detention.

00:07:02.919 --> 00:07:06.370
They're not allowed out on bail or they can't
afford it.

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:10.930
They're also being brainwashed as the cases
against them are going forward.

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:11.930
OK.

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:16.520
So overall, the prison sentences are getting
longer and longer.

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:21.370
In the last week, we saw the two longest prison
sentences of above 40 months.

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:26.669
The lesser charges for the Trump riders are
kind of being moved out of the way first,

00:07:26.669 --> 00:07:32.620
